myrmidon(1.6.5 REVIEW-REWORK-F02): the url branch of the delivering-task
lookup built `like ${"..."}%` — the wildcard sat outside the bound
parameter, so every call reached Postgres as `like $n%` and died with a
syntax error; the review-return loop was dead for tasks whose PR is
reachable only through a pull_request work-product url. The branch now
strips query/fragment parts and anchors on
/github.com/<repo>/pull/<number>(/|$), so /pull/12 and /pull/12/files
match PR 12 while /pull/123 no longer matches a search for 12. The
metadata repo/number branch is unchanged.

Adds:
- embedded-Postgres regression test
  server/src/myrmidon/review-rework/store.db.myrmidon.test.ts
- CI gate scripts/myrmidon/ci/sql-template-lint.mjs (+ node:test suite)
  flagging '%' glued to a sql-template interpolation edge across
  server/src, wired as a step in the checks job
- change fragment docs/myrmidon/changes/myr-1-6-5-review-rework-url-match.md

